 to be made address-independent (canonical dumps of header + every element + the *entire* hash index including all `hash[8]`/`index[8]` bucket arrays), and the element bytes the C leaves straight out of `realloc` are canonicalised — otherwise tests passed or failed depending on whether malloc handed back fresh zero pages.\n- `temp_key` is *never initialised* by `stbds_make_hash_index`, so it is only compared where the C has actually written it.\n\n**No Rust source changes were needed** — the translation matched the C on every input tested. To prove that isn't a vacuous result, I injected 19 mutations into `src/`: **17 detected, 2 provably equivalent mutants** (`n.wrapping_neg()` vs `unsigned_abs()` for `i32`; returning `a` where `a` is already NULL), 0 real escapes.\n\n`./run_all_configs.sh` automates the whole matrix (C build → feature enumeration → `cargo check` → build+test per profile → `nm -D` diff) and exits 0."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_read_input_tokens":286814,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":819,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42be0eca-3321-477d-b867-854c40f82f5c","uuid":"6c68efb7-d348-4c32-8e38-f1b3d62883a8","timestamp":"2026-08-20T06:05:58.073Z"}
